# DECISION: Approach A — purpose-built `vendor_service_time_slots` (with two corrections)

## Why A wins (scored against the six criteria)

| Criterion | A (own table) | B (reuse branches) | C (JSONB) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Correctness** | ✅ Models "time-bound slots" literally; each slot is a first-class row with its own capacity | ⚠️ Models *parallel lanes*, not *time*; `vendor_branches` is a billing/geo sub-account (`parent_vendor_profile_id` + `branch_subscription_active`), semantically wrong for "rooms" | ⚠️ Match is exact `slot_label` string equality, no time-range math; no shape/FK integrity |
| **Composition with #2** | ✅ Clean precedence rule (slots-present → #3, else #2), both hang off `targetVendor.service_id` at line 516 | ⚠️ "branches override daily_capacity" is a vendor-confusing parallel model; couples must own K service rows | ✅ Cleanest compose — both are columns on the same rows |
| **UX (couples + hotel rooms)** | ✅ Named windows per service ("AM Ceremony / PM Reception", "Grand Ballroom / Garden") fit the hotel case exactly | ⚠️ Forces a ₱999/28d branch subscription per "room" — wrong billing coupling | ⚠️ AM/PM only without a client island; >2 slots breaks the all-native-form purity |
| **Migration/RLS safety** | ✅ New table, RLS at CREATE copied verbatim from `vendor_branches` 264-279; helpers (`current_vendor_profile_ids`, `is_admin`, `current_event_ids`) all confirmed to exist | ✅ Reuses existing RLS (column adds) — its one real edge | ✅ No new RLS (column adds) — but **cross-row invariant unenforceable** (couple can stamp a `slot_label` that doesn't exist) |
| **Race robustness** | ✅ Only model that can get a real DB guard (`FOR UPDATE` RPC or per-date partial unique on `slot_capacity=1`) | ⚠️ Same TOCTOU as #2, no row to constrain cleanly | ❌ Worst — capacity lives in a blob, nothing to constrain; "oversell last slot" on a *paid* feature |
| **Build size** | ⚠️ Largest (new table + 2 actions + sub-editor) but bounded | ✅ Smallest (core variant = 1 column) **but only if "parallel lanes" is the requirement** | ✅ Small (2 columns) but pays it back in R1–R5 integrity debt |

**The deciding fact** (verified in `20260925000000_vendor_services_daily_capacity.sql`, the shipped #2 migration's own header): *"Enterprise time-bound slots (#3) layer a **separate time-of-day model** on top later."* The owner already committed to time-of-day, not parallel lanes. That rules B out as the primary (B answers "K parallel events/day", which #2's `daily_capacity` already covers for the photobooth case). C is forward-compatible but ships integrity/race debt on a *paid Enterprise* capability — unacceptable for revenue-bearing capacity. A is the only approach that models the literal requirement, composes cleanly with #2, and can be made race-safe.

**Two corrections applied to A as I'm specifying it:**
1. **Gate the editor on `slotsPerDay === Infinity` (Enterprise), not `slotsTimeBounded`.** `slotsTimeBounded` is `true` for **both** Pro and Enterprise (verified in `vendor-tier-caps.ts:43`). The brief says Enterprise-only, so the Enterprise signal is `slotsPerDay === Infinity`. (Open question #1 — owner may want Pro in.)
2. **Ship the atomic acquire RPC in the same PR**, not the read-then-write gate. The feature is paid; the existing #2 TOCTOU is a known free-feature gap, but A is the one model that can close it, so it should.

---

# BUILD SPEC — Enterprise time-bound slot plotting (#3)

## 1. Migration DDL (RLS at CREATE)

New file: `supabase/migrations/20261015000000_vendor_service_time_slots.sql`

```sql
-- ============================================================================
-- 20261015000000_vendor_service_time_slots.sql
-- Vendor tier feature #3 — Enterprise-only TIME-BOUND booking slots.
-- Canonical: Vendor_Tier_Capability_Matrix_2026-06-07.md. Delivers the
-- "separate time-of-day model on top" that 20260925000000_vendor_services_
-- daily_capacity.sql (#2) deferred.
--
-- An Enterprise vendor plots named per-service time windows ("AM Ceremony",
-- "Grand Ballroom"), each with its own per-day capacity. When a service has
-- >=1 active slot, finalizeVendor enforces PER-SLOT same-date counts and
-- SKIPS vendor_services.daily_capacity (#2). Services with zero slots keep #2.
--
-- Tier gate (slotsPerDay === Infinity = Enterprise) enforced APP-SIDE on
-- plot/edit (mirrors daily_capacity's app-side tier cap). SQL owns structural
-- CHECKs + RLS only.
-- ============================================================================

BEGIN;

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.vendor_service_time_slots (
  slot_id            UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  vendor_profile_id  UUID NOT NULL
                       REFERENCES public.vendor_profiles(vendor_profile_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  vendor_service_id  UUID NOT NULL
                       REFERENCES public.vendor_services(vendor_service_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  slot_label         TEXT NOT NULL
                       CHECK (length(slot_label) > 0 AND length(slot_label) <= 80),
  -- TIME, not TIMESTAMPTZ: a slot is a recurring window-of-day reused every date.
  start_time         TIME NOT NULL,
  end_time           TIME NOT NULL,
  slot_capacity      INT  NOT NULL DEFAULT 1
                       CHECK (slot_capacity > 0 AND slot_capacity <= 50),
  display_order      INT  NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  is_active          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,
  created_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

  CONSTRAINT vsts_window_ordered CHECK (end_time > start_time),
  CONSTRAINT vsts_start_granularity
    CHECK (EXTRACT(MINUTE FROM start_time) IN (0,30) AND EXTRACT(SECOND FROM start_time) = 0),
  CONSTRAINT vsts_end_granularity
    CHECK (EXTRACT(MINUTE FROM end_time)   IN (0,30) AND EXTRACT(SECOND FROM end_time)   = 0)
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS vsts_service_label_uniq
  ON public.vendor_service_time_slots (vendor_service_id, lower(slot_label))
  WHERE is_active;

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS vsts_service_active_idx
  ON public.vendor_service_time_slots (vendor_service_id, display_order, start_time)
  WHERE is_active;

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS vsts_owner_idx
  ON public.vendor_service_time_slots (vendor_profile_id);

COMMENT ON TABLE public.vendor_service_time_slots IS
  'Vendor tier feature #3 (Enterprise-only · owner 2026-06-07). Named per-service time windows, each with its own per-day capacity. When a service has >=1 active row, finalizeVendor enforces per-slot same-date counts and ignores vendor_services.daily_capacity (#2). Tier gate (slotsPerDay Infinity) enforced app-side. Time-of-day is the vendor''s operational partition; the wedding event itself is date-granular (events.event_date DATE).';

-- Booking -> slot binding (nullable; only set for slot-bearing services).
ALTER TABLE public.event_vendors
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS service_time_slot_id UUID NULL
    REFERENCES public.vendor_service_time_slots(slot_id) ON DELETE SET NULL;

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.event_vendors.service_time_slot_id IS
  'Tier #3: the time-bound slot this confirmed booking occupies. NULL for date-only / #2 bookings. ON DELETE SET NULL so deleting a slot degrades the booking to date-only, never orphans it.';

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS event_vendors_slot_status_idx
  ON public.event_vendors (service_time_slot_id, status)
  WHERE service_time_slot_id IS NOT NULL AND archived_at IS NULL;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- RLS at CREATE — copied verbatim from vendor_branches (20260530010000:264-279),
-- keyed on the local vendor_profile_id (vendor_branches keys parent_vendor_
-- profile_id; this table denormalizes vendor_profile_id, same idiom).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ALTER TABLE public.vendor_service_time_slots ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS vsts_vendor_access ON public.vendor_service_time_slots;
CREATE POLICY vsts_vendor_access
  ON public.vendor_service_time_slots FOR ALL
  TO authenticated
  USING (vendor_profile_id IN (SELECT public.current_vendor_profile_ids()))
  WITH CHECK (vendor_profile_id IN (SELECT public.current_vendor_profile_ids()));

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS vsts_admin_read ON public.vendor_service_time_slots;
CREATE POLICY vsts_admin_read
  ON public.vendor_service_time_slots FOR SELECT
  TO authenticated
  USING (public.is_admin());

-- Couple read: render the slot label on a booking they own. finalize WRITES
-- under the couple session (createClient()), so the booked-couple policy must
-- also allow the couple to SET service_time_slot_id on their own event_vendors
-- row — that write is governed by the existing event_vendors couple-write
-- policy (unchanged); this policy only adds SELECT on the slot row.
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS vsts_booked_couple_read ON public.vendor_service_time_slots;
CREATE POLICY vsts_booked_couple_read
  ON public.vendor_service_time_slots FOR SELECT
  TO authenticated
  USING (
    slot_id IN (
      SELECT ev.service_time_slot_id
      FROM public.event_vendors ev
      WHERE ev.event_id IN (SELECT public.current_event_ids())
        AND ev.service_time_slot_id IS NOT NULL
    )
  );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Atomic acquire RPC — closes the last-slot TOCTOU the read-then-write #2 gate
-- has (conflict_architecture memory). SECURITY DEFINER so it can lock + count
-- across events; validates caller owns the event via current_event_ids().
-- Returns the chosen slot_id, or NULL when all slots are full.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.acquire_service_time_slot(
  p_event_id   UUID,
  p_vendor_id  UUID,
  p_service_id UUID
) RETURNS UUID
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public
AS $$
DECLARE
  v_date          DATE;
  v_event_ids     UUID[];
  v_slot          RECORD;
  v_used          INT;
BEGIN
  -- Caller must own the event (RLS is bypassed under DEFINER, so check here).
  IF p_event_id NOT IN (SELECT public.current_event_ids()) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'not authorized for event %', p_event_id;
  END IF;

  SELECT event_date INTO v_date FROM public.events WHERE event_id = p_event_id;
  IF v_date IS NULL THEN
    RETURN NULL;  -- no date → degrade open (matches #2)
  END IF;

  SELECT array_agg(event_id) INTO v_event_ids
  FROM public.events WHERE event_date = v_date;

  -- Lock the candidate slot rows in deterministic order, first-open wins.
  FOR v_slot IN
    SELECT slot_id, slot_capacity
    FROM public.vendor_service_time_slots
    WHERE vendor_service_id = p_service_id AND is_active
    ORDER BY display_order, start_time
    FOR UPDATE
  LOOP
    SELECT count(*) INTO v_used
    FROM public.event_vendors
    WHERE service_time_slot_id = v_slot.slot_id
      AND status = 'contracted'
      AND archived_at IS NULL
      AND event_id = ANY (v_event_ids)
      AND vendor_id <> p_vendor_id;
    IF v_used < v_slot.slot_capacity THEN
      RETURN v_slot.slot_id;
    END IF;
  END LOOP;

  RETURN NULL;  -- all slots full
END;
$$;

REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION public.acquire_service_time_slot(UUID,UUID,UUID) FROM PUBLIC;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.acquire_service_time_slot(UUID,UUID,UUID) TO authenticated;

COMMIT;
```

> **Note on the RPC + `event_date` choice:** I deliberately read `events.event_date` (the **canonical write column**, verified at `20260513000000_iteration_0000_shell_schema.sql:108` as `DATE`), **not** `wedding_date`. The `wedding_date` generated mirror has **no `GENERATED ALWAYS` DDL in any tracked migration** (only a comment at shell-schema line 31) — confirmed by grep. The shipped #2 gate reads `wedding_date` and inherits that latent risk; the new RPC sidesteps it by reading `event_date`. See Open Question #2.

> The RPC uses `FOR UPDATE` to serialize concurrent finalizes on the same slot set — the real race fix that B/C cannot get. `'contracted'` matches `LOCKED_STATUS`.

